WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.841 --> 00:00:04.441
- Today, I'm going to share
what I did for Valentine's day.

00:00:04.441 --> 00:00:07.044
(whooshing)

00:00:07.044 --> 00:00:10.044
(Latin flare music)

00:00:13.851 --> 00:00:16.047
(scooter motor revving)

00:00:16.047 --> 00:00:19.449
So, it was recently
Valentine's day and in general

00:00:19.449 --> 00:00:23.684
I struggle with Valentine's
day because on the one hand

00:00:23.684 --> 00:00:27.957
I'm not a big fan of just
buying into made up holidays.

00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:29.970
And I like doing things just because.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.226
I would much rather do
something just because

00:00:32.226 --> 00:00:34.159
I feel like it has more meaning

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:35.983
than when you're forced to do something.

00:00:35.983 --> 00:00:37.348
And maybe just in general I don't like

00:00:37.348 --> 00:00:38.394
being forced to do anything.

00:00:38.394 --> 00:00:40.364
Maybe that like is at
the core of everything.

00:00:40.364 --> 00:00:42.642
As an entrepreneur,

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.849
don't put Evan in a box.

00:00:44.849 --> 00:00:47.043
I want do my own thing.

00:00:47.043 --> 00:00:48.222
Yeah, maybe that's probably at the core

00:00:48.222 --> 00:00:50.452
but on the other hand
I really like the idea

00:00:50.452 --> 00:00:52.234
of celebrating love.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.017
And so, every year I try to figure out

00:00:54.017 --> 00:00:55.459
something special to do.

00:00:55.459 --> 00:00:58.070
And so in past years I've
done cooking a meal for Nina,

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:59.319
getting everything setup for her,

00:00:59.319 --> 00:01:01.023
and surprising her at home.

00:01:01.023 --> 00:01:02.797
♫ When the moon hits your eye

00:01:02.797 --> 00:01:05.036
♫ Like a big pizza pie

00:01:05.036 --> 00:01:08.404
♫ That's amore

00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:09.884
I've also surprised her at work

00:01:09.884 --> 00:01:13.634
and showed up in a tie
that had hearts on it,

00:01:14.677 --> 00:01:16.760
and balloons and flowers.

00:01:17.899 --> 00:01:19.868
And I've given her presents
like I guess we all do

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:20.970
at different times.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.302
We give different presents.

00:01:22.302 --> 00:01:23.321
And I don't know,

00:01:23.321 --> 00:01:25.701
this year I felt like I
wanted to do something

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.132
a little more meaningful.

00:01:27.132 --> 00:01:29.166
I wanted to do something that had

00:01:29.166 --> 00:01:30.900
you know I wanted to do something that had

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:32.221
more lasting impact.

00:01:32.221 --> 00:01:34.939
I feel like if you just go
out to dinner at a restaurant

00:01:34.939 --> 00:01:37.587
it's kind of a lazy way out.

00:01:37.587 --> 00:01:39.427
It's kind of the expected thing to do

00:01:39.427 --> 00:01:41.612
and maybe yeah it's a great evening.

00:01:41.612 --> 00:01:43.460
But, it fades

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.430
and I wanted to do something
that had much more impact

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:48.151
that lasted a longer time.

00:01:48.151 --> 00:01:49.293
And so I was struggling.

00:01:49.293 --> 00:01:50.192
What do I do?

00:01:50.192 --> 00:01:52.114
What do I do that has that
deep meaningful impact.

00:01:52.114 --> 00:01:55.402
And my solution actually
cost zero dollars.

00:01:55.402 --> 00:01:56.951
It cost a ton of time

00:01:56.951 --> 00:01:59.324
but didn't cost me any money.

00:01:59.324 --> 00:02:03.221
What I ended up doing
was writing her a letter

00:02:03.221 --> 00:02:05.971
as to the reasons why I love her.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.642
And I thought back to when we
first started our relationship

00:02:10.642 --> 00:02:11.631
where we were just dating,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.945
and kind of worked out way
through up into the present day.

00:02:14.945 --> 00:02:18.977
All the different things that
I love about her and why.

00:02:18.977 --> 00:02:22.052
And I just wanted her to feel it

00:02:22.052 --> 00:02:25.543
as I was writing it I
started getting emotional.

00:02:25.543 --> 00:02:28.999
I had to take some breaks
and then come back to it.

00:02:28.999 --> 00:02:31.024
And she opened it at work

00:02:31.024 --> 00:02:32.982
and she read the first
paragraph and she started

00:02:32.982 --> 00:02:34.756
getting emotional,

00:02:34.756 --> 00:02:35.844
which is the goal, right?

00:02:35.844 --> 00:02:38.528
Like, deep meaningful
impact was the purpose

00:02:38.528 --> 00:02:40.057
that I wanted to have.

00:02:40.057 --> 00:02:41.724
And so she was reading
it and had to put it away

00:02:41.724 --> 00:02:42.987
and come back to it later

00:02:42.987 --> 00:02:45.522
so she's not crying at
her desk with co-workers

00:02:45.522 --> 00:02:47.387
kind of looking at what's going on.

00:02:47.387 --> 00:02:49.914
And it took me as I said a number of hours

00:02:49.914 --> 00:02:51.798
to put this thing together.

00:02:51.798 --> 00:02:53.055
In all honesty,

00:02:53.055 --> 00:02:57.259
it took me more time to do
that then to book a restaurant

00:02:57.259 --> 00:03:00.688
or to prepare a meal, or to cleanup,

00:03:00.688 --> 00:03:02.241
or to show up with flowers.

00:03:02.241 --> 00:03:04.033
You know any of the stuff
that I would have done.

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:05.872
It didn't cost me anything
in terms of dollars

00:03:05.872 --> 00:03:08.265
but cost me a lot in terms of time.

00:03:08.265 --> 00:03:12.151
Ended up having result that I wanted.

00:03:12.151 --> 00:03:14.315
I don't know what I'm
going to do next year.

00:03:14.315 --> 00:03:17.961
We'll see how I'm feeling
and go with that vibe there.

00:03:17.961 --> 00:03:19.851
But, I wanted to share it with you guys

00:03:19.851 --> 00:03:22.145
because I think a lot of times one,

00:03:22.145 --> 00:03:25.461
we do things maybe for the wrong reasons.

00:03:25.461 --> 00:03:28.229
We do things because we're
forced to do something

00:03:28.229 --> 00:03:31.803
or we do things that are at
a very superficial level.

00:03:31.803 --> 00:03:32.983
And then two,

00:03:32.983 --> 00:03:35.983
we feel like we have to do something

00:03:37.543 --> 00:03:40.006
just for somebody else's expectations.

00:03:40.006 --> 00:03:42.584
We need to go out and we
need to buy that thing

00:03:42.584 --> 00:03:45.371
and that's the thing that's
going to make that person happy.

00:03:45.371 --> 00:03:48.161
Right, I need to go out and
buy them this expensive present

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:49.656
for them to be happy.

00:03:49.656 --> 00:03:51.616
You may not be able to afford that thing.

00:03:51.616 --> 00:03:53.954
And really the results,

00:03:53.954 --> 00:03:55.810
the win you get from that present,

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.910
that super expensive gift,

00:03:57.910 --> 00:03:59.743
doesn't last you know?

00:04:00.764 --> 00:04:02.257
Doesn't have a long term impact

00:04:02.257 --> 00:04:05.479
and so what really touches peoples' hearts

00:04:05.479 --> 00:04:08.479
is that deep expression of gratitude

00:04:09.491 --> 00:04:10.978
and especially if it's somebody that

00:04:10.978 --> 00:04:13.123
you're in a relationship with.

00:04:13.123 --> 00:04:14.315
Why you love them.

00:04:14.315 --> 00:04:16.656
I'd encourage you to
try that our yourself.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.085
And you know what?

00:04:18.085 --> 00:04:19.690
This is a good challenge Believe Nation,

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.579
whether you're married or not,

00:04:21.579 --> 00:04:25.052
I want you to find
somebody in your life today

00:04:25.052 --> 00:04:28.671
who you just want to
express some thanks to.

00:04:28.671 --> 00:04:30.569
And either pick up the
phone and give them a call

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:33.485
or write them a nice letter
or send them an email.

00:04:33.485 --> 00:04:36.365
Just something really touching as to why

00:04:36.365 --> 00:04:38.984
they've impacted your life and how.

00:04:38.984 --> 00:04:40.814
I want you to feel the emotion.

00:04:40.814 --> 00:04:44.313
I want you to get choked
up in writing that email

00:04:44.313 --> 00:04:46.094
or in making that phone call

00:04:46.094 --> 00:04:48.753
to express how deeply this
person has impacted you.

00:04:48.753 --> 00:04:50.470
And again, it could be a friend,

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.721
it could a parent, it could
be a sibling, it could be,

00:04:52.721 --> 00:04:54.940
doesn't have to be your
spouse if you're not married.

00:04:54.940 --> 00:04:57.707
I want you to get choked
up in writing that message.

00:04:57.707 --> 00:04:59.947
And if you do that

00:04:59.947 --> 00:05:02.072
they're probably going
to get choked up, too.

00:05:02.072 --> 00:05:03.755
They're probably going
to really appreciate you

00:05:03.755 --> 00:05:05.149
for writing that message.

00:05:05.149 --> 00:05:07.006
And even if they don't,

00:05:07.006 --> 00:05:09.235
worse case scenario,

00:05:09.235 --> 00:05:11.028
it's still a gift.

00:05:11.028 --> 00:05:12.941
You writing that the
intention is positive.

00:05:12.941 --> 00:05:14.295
It's still a gift.

00:05:14.295 --> 00:05:16.229
And so I'd love to challenge you today

00:05:16.229 --> 00:05:20.037
as we close the weekend to
send somebody a nice message

00:05:20.037 --> 00:05:22.245
of how they've impacted you.

00:05:22.245 --> 00:05:24.714
And I guarantee you're
going to feel good about it

00:05:24.714 --> 00:05:26.241
and hopefully so will they.

00:05:26.241 --> 00:05:27.299
That's it.

00:05:27.299 --> 00:05:28.720
Hope you guys have a great weekend.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.020
I believe in you.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.766
Continue to believe in yourself.

00:05:31.766 --> 00:05:33.848
And whatever your one word is,

00:05:33.848 --> 00:05:34.681
much love.

00:05:35.938 --> 00:05:37.021
See you soon.

